.TH LZFSE 1 "September 2026" "TdeZip Tools" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
lzfse \- LZFSE lossless data compression utility
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B lzfse
[\fB\-encode\fR|\fB\-decode\fR|\fB\-d\fR|\fB\-t\fR] [\fB\-i\fR \fIinput\fR] [\fB\-o\fR \fIoutput\fR] [\fB\-v\fR]
.br
.B lzfse
[\fB\-d\fR|\fB\-t\fR] [\fIinput\fR] [\fB\-o\fR \fIoutput\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B lzfse
is a lossless data compression tool using the LZFSE algorithm developed by Apple Inc.
It combines a Lempel-Ziv sliding window technique with Finite State Entropy (FSE) coding.
It provides compression ratios comparable to Deflate/zlib while offering significantly
faster compression and decompression speeds with lower energy consumption.
.PP
When used without arguments or in pipelines,
.B lzfse
reads from standard input and writes to standard output, making it suitable for use
with GNU
.BR tar (1)
via the \fB\-\-use\-compress\-program\fR option.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-encode, \-c, \-z
Compress the input data.
.TP
.B \-decode, \-d, \-\-decompress
Decompress the input data.
.TP
.B \-t, \-\-test
Test the integrity of the compressed file without writing output to disk.
.TP
.B \-i \fIfile\fR
Specify input file (defaults to standard input).
.TP
.B \-o \fIfile\fR
Specify output file (defaults to standard output).
.TP
.B \-f, \-\-force
Force overwrite of existing output files.
.TP
.B \-v, \-\-verbose
Display compression statistics and throughput.
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Display command usage summary.
